# Forge IDE environment
#
# Both variables are optional. With neither set, the app boots in Local
# Development Mode: authentication issues a browser-local account and every
# project lives in IndexedDB. Nothing crashes and no feature silently misleads
# you — the UI labels the mode.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values. Never commit `.env`.
#
# The values below point at one specific Supabase project. They are a working
# example, not a default: a fresh clone that leaves them in place will read and
# write that project's database rather than its own. Replace both before you
# run this anywhere real. (The anon key is safe to publish — it grants nothing
# on its own — but the project it names is still somebody's.)

# Your Supabase project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklm.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://awgdurlvfqxtdadpuzse.supabase.co

# The Supabase anon (publishable) key.
#
# This key is embedded in the client bundle, which is safe by design: it grants
# nothing on its own, because every table is protected by row level security.
#
# NEVER put the service-role key here. It bypasses RLS entirely, and anything
# prefixed VITE_ ends up in JavaScript that every visitor downloads. Forge
# refuses to start with a service-role key and logs an error instead.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImF3Z2R1cmx2ZnF4dGRhZHB1enNlIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODcyMzk4MzEsImV4cCI6MjEwMjgxNTgzMX0.EAT7SLa9ydLrORRY0K6wzz4hV7gpQSFIf3D59XHkFIc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub integration (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Nothing below belongs in this file. The GitHub OAuth client secret is a
# server-side secret, and anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into JavaScript
# every visitor downloads — so the browser never receives it.
#
# Set these as Supabase Edge Function secrets instead:
#
#   supabase secrets set GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=...
#   supabase secrets set GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=...
#   supabase secrets set FORGE_APP_ORIGIN=https://your-forge-deployment.example
#   supabase secrets set GITHUB_OAUTH_SCOPES="repo read:user"   # optional
#
# then deploy the functions that use them:
#
#   supabase functions deploy github-oauth
#   supabase functions deploy github-proxy
#
# Register the OAuth app on GitHub with the callback URL
# <FORGE_APP_ORIGIN>/settings/github/callback.
#
# Without Supabase, Forge runs in Local Development Mode and GitHub is reached
# directly from the browser with a personal access token you paste into
# Settings → Integrations. That token is held in sessionStorage for the tab
# only. It is the honest local fallback, not the deployment posture.
